  "goodToKnow": "Der Knabe is an old-fashioned or literary word for boy; today people say der Junge. It survives in fixed terms: der Knabenchor (boys' choir), like the Thomanerchor in Leipzig, founded in 1212, whose cantor was once Bach. Humorously, ein alter Knabe means an old boy. Goethe's poem Heidenröslein begins Sah ein Knab' ein Röslein stehn. Weak noun: den Knaben. Plural: die Knaben."
